From 500854b1762654f99f23d41df437b89d6025a1de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:59:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] crypto/store/store_result.c: fix EVP_SKEYMGMT leak in
 try_skey()

When a store loader returns a symmetric key by reference, try_skey()
fetches the SKEYMGMT from the loader's provider and passes
it to EVP_SKEY_import_SKEYMGMT().  The new EVP_SKEY takes its own
reference, so the reference from the fetch was never released.
That leaked one EVP_SKEYMGMT per secret key loaded,
e.g. with "openssl storeutl pkcs11:" through pkcs11-provider.

Fixes: 1b0f21f0555c "Implementing store support for EVP_SKEY"
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Simo Sorce <simo@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Belyavskiy <beldmit@gmail.com>
Merge-date: Thu Nov 12 10:17:59 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33643
(cherry picked from commit 3e16cec66849b90ed0f922310c7b04b49f7c602e)
---
 crypto/store/store_result.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crypto/store/store_result.c b/crypto/store/store_result.c
index a47eb2a..726b756 100644
--- a/crypto/store/store_result.c
+++ b/crypto/store/store_result.c
@@ -709,6 +709,8 @@ static int try_skey(struct extracted_param_data_st *data, OSSL_STORE_INFO **v,
         params[1] = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
 
         skey = EVP_SKEY_import_SKEYMGMT(libctx, skeymgmt, OSSL_SKEYMGMT_SELECT_ALL, params);
+        /* The EVP_SKEY holds its own reference to the SKEYMGMT */
+        EVP_SKEYMGMT_free(skeymgmt);
     }
 
     if (skey != NULL)
